  "standing": "\u001b[1;90mSTANDING HEXAGRAM 63:\n\n\u001b[0m(Line at bottom is first)\n\n  \u001b[1;97m8  ━━━   ━━━  \u001b[0m（上, 6th）──┐\n  \u001b[1;97m7  ━━━━━━━━━  \u001b[0m（五, 5th）──┼── 水（上卦）\n  \u001b[1;97m8  ━━━   ━━━  \u001b[0m（四, 4th）──┘   Water, as in rain, clouds, springs, streams and defiles. The moon (upper trigram)\n  \u001b[1;97m7  ━━━━━━━━━  \u001b[0m（三, 3rd）──┐\n  \u001b[1;97m8  ━━━   ━━━  \u001b[0m（二, 2nd）──┼── 火（下卦）\n  \u001b[1;97m7  ━━━━━━━━━  \u001b[0m（初, 1st）──┘   Fire, as in lightning; the sun (lower trigram)\n\n\u001b[0m(First is line at bottom)\n\n  \u001b[1;97m7, \u001b[1;97m8, \u001b[1;97m7, \u001b[1;97m8, \u001b[1;97m7, \u001b[1;97m8\n\n\u001b[1;90mSTANDING HEXAGRAM NAME:\n\n\u001b[90m[武英殿本]\n\n  \u001b[1;97m既濟\n\n\u001b[90m[Legge]\n\n  \u001b[1;97mLXIII. The Kî Žî Hexagram\n\n\n\u001b[1;90mSTANDING HEXAGRAM STRUCTURE:\n\n  \u001b[90m互卦 Nuclear Hexagram:  \u001b[1;97m#64 未濟 / LXIV. The Wei Žî Hexagram\u001b[0m\n  \u001b[90m錯卦 Inverse Hexagram:  \u001b[1;97m#64 未濟 / LXIV. The Wei Žî Hexagram\u001b[0m\n  \u001b[90m綜卦 Reversed Hexagram: \u001b[1;97m#64 未濟 / LXIV. The Wei Žî Hexagram\u001b[0m\n\n\n\u001b[1;90m卦辭:\n\u001b[90m[武英殿本]\n\n  \u001b[1;97m既濟：亨，小利貞，初吉終亂。\n\n\u001b[90m[Legge]\n\n  \u001b[1;97mKî Žî intimates progress and success in small matters. There will be advantage in being firm and correct. There has been good fortune in the beginning; there may be disorder in the end.\n\n\u001b[1;90m大象:\n\u001b[90m[武英殿本]\n\n  \u001b[1;97m水在火上，既濟；君子以思患而預防之。\n\n\u001b[90m[Legge]\n\n  \u001b[1;97mLXIII. (The trigram representing) fire and that for water above it form Kî Žî. The superiorman, in accordance with this, thinks of evil (that may come), and beforehand guards against it.",
  "emerging": "\u001b[1;90mEMERGING HEXAGRAM 63:\n\n\u001b[0m(Line at bottom is first)\n\n  \u001b[1;97m8  ━━━   ━━━  \u001b[0m（上, 6th）──┐\n  \u001b[1;97m7  ━━━━━━━━━  \u001b[0m（五, 5th）──┼── 水（上卦）\n  \u001b[1;97m8  ━━━   ━━━  \u001b[0m（四, 4th）──┘   Water, as in rain, clouds, springs, streams and defiles. The moon (upper trigram)\n  \u001b[1;97m7  ━━━━━━━━━  \u001b[0m（三, 3rd）──┐\n  \u001b[1;97m8  ━━━   ━━━  \u001b[0m（二, 2nd）──┼── 火（下卦）\n  \u001b[1;97m7  ━━━━━━━━━  \u001b[0m（初, 1st）──┘   Fire, as in lightning; the sun (lower trigram)\n\n\u001b[0m(First is line at bottom)\n\n  \u001b[1;97m7, \u001b[1;97m8, \u001b[1;97m7, \u001b[1;97m8, \u001b[1;97m7, \u001b[1;97m8\n\n\u001b[1;90mEMERGING HEXAGRAM NAME:\n\n\u001b[90m[武英殿本]\n\n  \u001b[1;97m既濟\n\n\u001b[90m[Legge]\n\n  \u001b[1;97mLXIII. The Kî Žî Hexagram\n\n\n\u001b[1;90mEMERGING HEXAGRAM STRUCTURE:\n\n  \u001b[90m互卦 Nuclear Hexagram:  \u001b[1;97m#64 未濟 / LXIV. The Wei Žî Hexagram\u001b[0m\n  \u001b[90m錯卦 Inverse Hexagram:  \u001b[1;97m#64 未濟 / LXIV. The Wei Žî Hexagram\u001b[0m\n  \u001b[90m綜卦 Reversed Hexagram: \u001b[1;97m#64 未濟 / LXIV. The Wei Žî Hexagram\u001b[0m\n\n\n\u001b[1;90mEDITIONS AND WITNESSES:\n\n\u001b[90m[武英殿本]\n\n  \u001b[1;97m武英殿十三經注疏本《周易正義》 (1739)\n  \u001b[0mWitness: ctext.org's transcription of the 武英殿十三經注疏本《周易正義》, from its Book of Changes pages (ctext.org/book-of-changes); the 乾 and 坤 pages (用九, 用六) retrieved 2026-11-27\n\n\u001b[90m[Legge]\n\n  \u001b[1;97mLegge, Sacred Books of the East vol. 16 (Oxford, 1882)\n  \u001b[0mWitness: a scanned copy of Sacred Books of the East vol. 16 (1882); the 乾 and 坤 pages: pp. 58, 61 (text) and 267, 269 (小象)"
